WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:07.799
♪♪♪ Weighty, rhythmic tones ♪♪♪

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:09.217
- [Naomi Graham:] The best thing about boxing

00:00:09.217 --> 00:00:10.885
is just the sweet science.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:13.013
It's a mental thing.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:16.808
I love the hard work.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.852
When I am winning,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.188
I know that those nights being homeless,

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.440
being bullied,

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.858
and everything that I have been through

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.443
will always be with me.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.113
Going out there,

00:00:30.113 --> 00:00:32.907
I don't really have any fears or any doubts

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:34.242
because I know the only person

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:35.744
that can beat me is me.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.371
And I will never forget

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.415
what it took to get there.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:46.463
♪♪♪ Slow keyboard and beats ♪♪♪

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:48.339
My name is Naomi Graham.

00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:49.924
I'm from Fayetteville, North Carolina,

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:51.468
and I'm a boxer for Team USA.

00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:55.013
I compete in middleweight,

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:58.016
which is 165 pounds, 75 kilograms.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.312
And I like to consider my style very unique.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.523
I don't just compete one way.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:10.945
♪♪♪ Upbeat ♪♪♪

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:13.698
- [Announcer:] Naomiii Graham!

00:01:13.698 --> 00:01:15.283
- I can box and move.

00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:16.785
I can walk you down.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:18.703
And I feel like I have a really good jab.

00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:23.958
- [Voiceover:] My name is Billy Walsh.

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:26.419
I'm head coach of USA Boxing team.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.297
To become a boxer within this program,

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:31.299
a boxer has got to have many, many qualities.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:32.884
Not only do you need to be able to fight,

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:34.552
but you need to have a good lifestyle.

00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:36.721
We've got, you know, plenty of structure.

00:01:36.721 --> 00:01:39.057
♪♪♪ Upbeat beats ♪♪♪

00:01:39.057 --> 00:01:41.559
- [Graham:] A day in camp for Team USA looks like

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:45.063
waking up at seven, weighing in, training,

00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:47.357
eating and doing strength and conditioning,

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:50.235
training again and going to bed about nine.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.992
- [Walsh:] Most of the kids that's in this program

00:01:57.992 --> 00:02:00.411
started boxing at seven and eight years of age.

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:02.413
So they've been boxing a helluva long time.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:03.915
There is the exception to the rule.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.876
- [Graham:] I'm 30 years old,

00:02:06.876 --> 00:02:10.672
and when I started boxing, I was 22 years old.

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:13.174
My mother, she looked at me as being fragile,

00:02:13.174 --> 00:02:14.884
her baby, the youngest.

00:02:14.884 --> 00:02:16.886
She didn't really want me to box.

00:02:16.886 --> 00:02:24.018
♪♪♪ Contemplative tones ♪♪♪

00:02:24.018 --> 00:02:27.480
- I'm sitting out on the front porch at my house,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.440
where Naomi grew up.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.443
We been here about 20 years, I guess.

00:02:32.443 --> 00:02:34.529
My name is Bertha Clark.

00:02:34.529 --> 00:02:37.699
I'm living in Fayetteville, North Carolina.

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:41.494
Naomi is my sixth child.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.288
She's my baby, you know,

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:47.041
and when she got into that profession, boxing,

00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:49.836
you know, I wasn't for it at first.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.547
- [Graham:] My mother was a single parent.

00:02:52.547 --> 00:02:55.675
She put in a lot of hours to take care of six kids.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.720
- [Clark:] I was a battered, bruised wife.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.055
But God delivered me out of that.

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:04.100
And, uh, the children—we come through together,

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.978
you know. And we gon—we risin' together.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.815
- [Graham:] Fayetteville is a military town.

00:03:10.815 --> 00:03:12.358
It's pretty quiet.

00:03:13.902 --> 00:03:15.987
There's a lot of boxing gyms to go to,

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:18.740
and that's where I spent a lot of my time

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.326
following my sister Rachel to her practices.

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:23.328
A lot of times I saw

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:25.914
the blood, sweat and tears she put into it,

00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:27.373
and I wanted that.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.709
I wanted something to drive me

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:31.961
just as much as it was driving her.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.631
- [Clark:] When you believe something

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:36.633
and you got faith in your heart,

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:39.344
that you goin' do it and you put work toward it?

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:40.637
You goin' make it.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.055
- [Graham:] Being the youngest,

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.890
I spent a lot of time to myself.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.099
For many years,

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:47.227
I was bullied because I was so quiet.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.687
And my mother believed that

00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:51.272
that if someone is picking on you,

00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:52.607
you just tell the teacher

00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:54.275
—you don't engage with the student.

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:55.526
So because of that,

00:03:55.526 --> 00:03:57.904
I also got picked on even more.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:01.115
One time, I was forced to fight back, but

00:04:01.115 --> 00:04:04.035
I don't consider myself violent outside of the ring.

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:06.246
Inside of the ring, it's a chess match.

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.872
It's, it's more strategic.

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:09.499
It's, it's not about violence.

00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:12.210
♪♪♪ I got what it takes / I will never break /

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.629
Always goin' hard / No matter what they say /

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:17.674
Man, I got what it takes / I will never break /

00:04:17.674 --> 00:04:21.094
Always goin' hard / No matter what they say ♪♪♪

00:04:21.511 --> 00:04:22.679
My next competition is

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:24.722
the Pan American Games in Lima, Peru.

00:04:24.722 --> 00:04:25.974
- [Walsh:] These Games in particular

00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:27.475
are important for Naomi.

00:04:27.475 --> 00:04:28.476
In boxing terms,

00:04:28.476 --> 00:04:30.603
it's the third-largest in the world.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.938
You've got the Pan Ams, then we got the

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.773
world championships, then we got Olympic Games.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.150
- Bienvenidos al Coliseo Miguel Grau.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:40.947
♪♪♪ Upbeat vibes ♪♪♪

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.115
[Graham:] There should be three fights

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.449
Each fight that you win,

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.159
you would go to the next level, and

00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:46.869
the third fight should be the finals.

00:04:49.163 --> 00:04:50.164
I'm in Lima, Peru,

00:04:50.164 --> 00:04:51.916
and I've been here almost a week.

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:53.167
I'm feeling very confident

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.168
about this tournament.

00:04:54.168 --> 00:04:55.378
I'm excited.

00:04:55.378 --> 00:04:57.380
I'm ready to go ahead and get gold.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.423
I'm excited.

00:04:58.423 --> 00:05:00.967
- [Announcer:] Atención: Estados Unidos,

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.177
categoría setenta y cinco kilos,

00:05:03.177 --> 00:05:04.220
cuartos de final.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.849
- [Second Announcer:] Naomi Graham!

00:05:10.184 --> 00:05:16.607
♪♪♪ Rock guitar ♪♪♪

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:19.402
The winner, in the blue corner,

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:21.654
from the USA…

00:05:26.409 --> 00:05:30.330
Naomiii Graaaham!

00:05:33.374 --> 00:05:35.376
- [Graham:] The hardest part of training

00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:36.669
is the mental.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.671
You could be the most talented boxer,

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.631
but if you're not there mentally,

00:05:40.631 --> 00:05:42.300
you can't be successful.

00:05:43.217 --> 00:05:45.553
I've always been that type of person to

00:05:45.553 --> 00:05:46.846
—any adversity

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.806
or any problems or difficulties,

00:05:48.806 --> 00:05:50.391
I feel like I need to handle them on my own.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.602
I became homeless

00:05:52.602 --> 00:05:54.437
when I was 21.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.731
My mother decided that

00:05:56.731 --> 00:05:59.567
I needed to get myself together and

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.235
figure it out on my own.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.404
I found a home that was abandoned,

00:06:03.404 --> 00:06:04.572
and that's where I stayed,

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:05.698
mostly in the back room.

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:06.866
Mostly at night

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.493
is when I would go by the home.

00:06:08.993 --> 00:06:10.328
I didn't know where I wanted to go,

00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:11.829
what I was going to do with my life,

00:06:11.829 --> 00:06:12.663
and I didn't know

00:06:12.663 --> 00:06:14.332
what was the next step from there.

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:16.834
A lot of the nights,

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.127
I was in deep thought...

00:06:18.127 --> 00:06:20.129
of what I really wanted for myself

00:06:20.129 --> 00:06:21.714
and the person that I wanted to be.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.675
A lot of my decisions were made

00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:26.636
in the dark in the abandoned home.

00:06:28.137 --> 00:06:29.597
The last night

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:32.058
that I spent in the home, homeless,

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:33.309
I was in the back room,

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:34.352
and I said,

00:06:34.352 --> 00:06:36.020
"This is it. You're gonna be bigger

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:38.356
than anyone else expected you to be."

00:06:38.356 --> 00:06:48.032
♪♪♪ Serious beats and tones ♪♪♪

00:06:48.032 --> 00:06:50.660
Yesterday I got a second-round TKO,

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.162
which is the stoppage, a win against Mexico.

00:06:55.456 --> 00:06:57.125
Now that I got the win yesterday,

00:06:57.125 --> 00:06:59.460
I am preparing for the semifinals against Brazil,

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:00.753
tomorrow the 30th.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:08.803
[Cheering and sounds from the crowd]

00:07:08.803 --> 00:07:10.721
- [Second Announcer:] In the blue corner,

00:07:10.721 --> 00:07:16.936
for the USA, Naomiii Graaaham!

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.480
♪♪♪ Contemplative tones ♪♪♪

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.023
- [Graham:] The first step to changing my life

00:07:21.023 --> 00:07:23.651
after I was homeless was joining the Army.

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.654
My first duty station was here

00:07:26.654 --> 00:07:28.364
in Colorado Springs, Colorado.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.741
Colorado Springs is where

00:07:30.741 --> 00:07:32.535
Team USA trains for boxing,

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:34.162
but I didn't know that at the time

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:35.455
that I got stationed here.

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.457
I said that I would just train on my own.

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:40.001
Someone saw me in a gym,

00:07:40.001 --> 00:07:41.669
and they said, "Well, you're in the military.

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:43.254
You should go to All-Army."

00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:44.547
So I went there,

00:07:44.547 --> 00:07:47.383
and you have to either beat a WCAP member

00:07:47.383 --> 00:07:48.551
and then place a top four

00:07:48.551 --> 00:07:50.136
at a national tournament.

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:51.429
I did both.

00:07:51.429 --> 00:07:54.056
The first yes that I received was from WCAP.

00:07:54.056 --> 00:07:58.102
♪♪♪

00:07:58.102 --> 00:08:00.062
This is the World Class Athlete Program.

00:08:00.062 --> 00:08:02.148
This is actually where everything started,

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:03.900
and this is where I'm training

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.401
when I'm not with Team USA.

00:08:05.401 --> 00:08:09.071
A lot of hours spent on the speed bags.

00:08:10.239 --> 00:08:10.907
This is where

00:08:10.907 --> 00:08:12.909
the blood, sweat and tears started.

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:14.410
It was very painful. [Laughing]

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:21.792
[Crowd cheering]

00:08:21.792 --> 00:08:23.336
- [Voiceover:] My name is Joe Guzman,

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:25.546
and I'm one of the volunteer coaches

00:08:25.546 --> 00:08:27.131
with the national boxing team.

00:08:27.131 --> 00:08:30.343
So I met Naomi Graham about five or six years ago.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:31.969
I was working as one of the assistant coaches

00:08:31.969 --> 00:08:33.387
in the World Class Athlete Program.

00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:34.639
[Graham:] I would be on the bag

00:08:34.639 --> 00:08:36.057
and saw him kind of looking at me,

00:08:36.057 --> 00:08:37.183
and he was saying,

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.768
you know, "Do you have any fights?"

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:40.186
You know, "I see potential in you."

00:08:41.687 --> 00:08:42.772
- [Guzman:] One thing that

00:08:42.772 --> 00:08:44.148
really stood out to me

00:08:44.148 --> 00:08:46.400
from the beginning was just her work ethic.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.777
You know, everything she did,

00:08:47.777 --> 00:08:49.320
she did at, like, 100 percent.

00:08:49.737 --> 00:08:50.821
- [Graham:] Coach Guzman—

00:08:50.821 --> 00:08:52.323
he was very important

00:08:52.323 --> 00:08:53.574
to me learning myself

00:08:53.574 --> 00:08:54.408
as a boxer,

00:08:54.408 --> 00:08:55.910
to—what it would take

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.495
to be on top.

00:08:57.495 --> 00:08:59.163
My highest point in WCAP

00:08:59.163 --> 00:09:02.917
was when I won the 2017 national championships.

00:09:02.917 --> 00:09:05.336
Once you win a national title,

00:09:05.336 --> 00:09:07.588
you're automatically on Team USA

00:09:07.588 --> 00:09:08.756
from that moment on.

00:09:08.756 --> 00:09:16.222
♪♪♪ Driving beats ♪♪♪

00:09:16.222 --> 00:09:17.932
Tomorrow is the gold-medal bout,

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:20.268
and I will be competing against Colombia.

00:09:20.268 --> 00:09:21.811
She's more of an aggressive fighter,

00:09:21.811 --> 00:09:23.437
so I'm definitely gonna have to work my jab

00:09:23.437 --> 00:09:25.648
a lot with her and stay to my right.

00:09:34.657 --> 00:09:36.200
- [Second Announcer:] The winner on points and

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:41.872
women's middleweight, 75-kilogram gold medalist,

00:09:41.872 --> 00:09:47.545
in the red corner, from Colombiaaa…

00:09:47.545 --> 00:10:00.266
♪♪♪ Fight / Fight / Fight /

00:10:00.266 --> 00:10:08.065
Stand up and fight / Fight ♪♪♪

00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:13.112
- [Clark:] Sometimes,

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:16.532
if you don't push your child out,

00:10:16.532 --> 00:10:19.118
then you're hindering them.

00:10:19.118 --> 00:10:22.330
Sometimes, in life,

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:25.166
you need that struggle,

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.461
you need that wrassle, you know.

00:10:28.461 --> 00:10:29.587
So you can know

00:10:29.587 --> 00:10:31.172
just how much to take

00:10:31.172 --> 00:10:33.424
or which direction you want to go.

00:10:33.424 --> 00:10:34.759
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:10:37.511 --> 00:10:38.929
- [Graham:] If it wasn't for my mother,

00:10:38.929 --> 00:10:41.807
I couldn't possibly be where I am today.

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:43.267
She showed me,

00:10:43.267 --> 00:10:44.560
you know, that she was tough

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:45.561
all my life.

00:10:46.187 --> 00:10:49.023
- What Naomi's doing now

00:10:49.023 --> 00:10:50.983
pleases me because

00:10:50.983 --> 00:10:53.694
she spoke it back in the past

00:10:53.694 --> 00:10:57.198
and it's coming to manifestation.

00:10:57.198 --> 00:10:59.533
And nobody

00:10:59.533 --> 00:11:02.995
can get where Naomi's at without hard work,

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:05.247
without some sacrifices,

00:11:05.247 --> 00:11:06.999
without some pain.

00:11:07.875 --> 00:11:09.710
- [Graham:] My tattoo is actually of my mother,

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.629
and I just want to take her everywhere that I go.

00:11:13.089 --> 00:11:14.548
My right arm is my strong arm.

00:11:14.548 --> 00:11:15.841
That's another reason why I got my tattoo

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:16.842
on my right arm.

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:20.346
- [Walsh:] I think boxing, you know,

00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:23.224
really, really tests your character.

00:11:23.224 --> 00:11:25.393
I think it actually builds character,

00:11:25.393 --> 00:11:27.269
tests everything that you have inside of you,

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:30.064
you know, and I think it teaches you discipline,

00:11:30.064 --> 00:11:32.316
you know, and it teaches you manners.

00:11:32.316 --> 00:11:34.276
And it gives you a lot of qualities that will

00:11:34.276 --> 00:11:35.903
withstand you in life.

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:38.239
- [Guzman:] The last five years for Graham,

00:11:38.239 --> 00:11:40.491
I mean, she's really stepped it up.

00:11:40.491 --> 00:11:41.951
So I mean, she's on a great path

00:11:41.951 --> 00:11:43.703
of making this Olympic team, for sure.

00:11:44.995 --> 00:11:46.038
- [Graham:] My ultimate goal

00:11:46.038 --> 00:11:48.624
is to go to the Olympics and win gold.

00:11:48.624 --> 00:11:50.084
The sky is the limit.

00:11:50.084 --> 00:11:51.544
And anything that you want to be in life,

00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:52.336
you can do that.

00:11:52.336 --> 00:11:53.713
And I want to show everybody

00:11:53.713 --> 00:11:55.506
that no matter what you're going through,

00:11:55.506 --> 00:11:57.633
no matter anything that happens in your life,

00:11:57.633 --> 00:11:59.260
you can be whatever you want to be.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:04.223
♪♪♪ Weighty, rhythmic tones ♪♪♪

00:12:04.223 --> 00:12:12.773
♪♪♪ Staccato synth ♪♪♪

00:12:12.773 --> 00:12:21.866
[Forceful exhalations with each punch]

00:12:30.082 --> 00:12:31.751
- [Lisa Leslie:] Hi, Naomi. [Laughing]

00:12:31.751 --> 00:12:32.918
- [Graham:] Oh, my god.

00:12:33.127 --> 00:12:34.086
- [Leslie:] Surprise!

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:35.087
- [Graham:] [Laughing]

00:12:35.713 --> 00:12:37.173
- [Leslie:] Are you OK?

